WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
January six, House committee

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.769
member Republican Congressman

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.636
Adam Kinzinger.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.137
Congressman,

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.205
thanks so much for joining us.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.506
Trump was taken off

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.440
Twitter in the first place

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.309
for inciting the violent insurrection

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.143
against the Capitol.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.444
You're a member of the committee

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.946
investigating the insurrection.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.080
What do you make of Elon

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.217
Musk reinstating Donald Trump

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.352
Well, look, I mean, I get that

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.920
people are on all sides of this debate.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.955
And the fact that he did it

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.523
with a poll of which,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.257
you know, however

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.158
many percent of those

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.026
could have been bots

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.628
that aren't real people voting in that.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.764
Secondarily, I don't know if,

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.831
you know, that decision

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.333
should be made by some poll.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.201
I mean, what happened?

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.170
I remember specifically

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:37.937
when this was all done.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.572
So not only was he lighting

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.409
and accelerating the fire on January six,

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.176
also before

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.512
January six with his conspiracies

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.679
at the end of the day,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.882
he said this is what you get

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.484
when a victory is so unceremoniously

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.519
basically taken away

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.820
from the American people.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.655
So not only when it was done.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.723
Did he have any remorse?

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:57.424
He said,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.091
well, of course,

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.325
you guys had an insurrection

00:00:59.325 --> 00:00:59.993
because that's what you get

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.294
when you steal an election.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:01.561
I mean,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.430
I remember seeing that specific tweet

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.632
and just being outraged

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.600
at how after all this is done,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.002
can you still do that?

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.170
And so now this idea

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:10.637
that he's going to

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.704
come on and be reformed,

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.906
everybody knows he won't.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.641
And by the way, I say, as a quick

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.742
aside, the person

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.709
probably the most upset

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:17.911
today is Devin Nunes,

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.245
because this is going to tank

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.748
truth social if he does, in fact, leave.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.149
On Friday, Attorney General Merrick

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.884
Garland appointed a special counsel

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.020
to oversee the investigations

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.754
into Donald Trump's

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.222
handling of classified documents,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.890
as well as the one

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.591
looking at his role

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.792
in the January six insurrection.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.661
You have expressed frustration

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.463
with the Justice Department's approach

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.931
to Trump in the past.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.165
Do you think this is the right move

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.169
You know, I'm going to have to leave

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.904
that to the experts to decide

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.573
if this was the right thing,

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.207
because I don't know where

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.041
the Justice Department

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.209
is in their investigation.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.643
Let's say, for instance,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.145
they were very close to indictment

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.080
and then they switched to this

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.381
because he's running for office.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.217
And I think that's an unnecessary delay.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.651
But then again,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.752
if we're trying to do the best

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.688
we can to take politics out of it.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.188
First off,

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.056
there are a lot of people

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.157
that will never be satisfied

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.258
that there's no politics

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.127
because that's how they frankly

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:07.794
raise money

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.662
is to to convince people

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.831
that there are some conspiracy out there.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.565
But I think what

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.800
we're going to be able to judge us by

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.568
is what the ultimate outcome is.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.070
Will he will

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.471
this special prosecutor

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.507
get to our independent counsel, get to a

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.076
belief that he

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:23.643
was guilty or

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.211
not, will be based on the evidence

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.279
and what will be the result

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:26.846
of Donald Trump?

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:27.180
But look,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.882
if the former president thinks

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:29.382
that just

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.350
by simply announcing

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.618
he's running for president,

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.386
he can obstruct justice.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.355
I mean, that would be a bad precedent,

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:35.655
of course,

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:35.955
because then

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.524
anybody that's under investigation

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.224
could just announce

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:38.591
they're running

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.226
for president in this country.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.528
The January six committee

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.662
is going to wrap up its work

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.463
by the end of the year,

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.297
and it seems likely

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.498
you'll have to do so

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.366
without hearing

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.401
from former Vice President Mike Pence.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.802
Here's what he told me about that

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.638
a few days ago.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.541
Congress has no right to my testimony.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.876
The very notion of a committee

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.710
on Congress

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.411
in Congress

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.812
summoning a vice president

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.614
to speak about deliberations

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.916
that took place at the White House,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.552
I think would violate the separation

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.219
of powers.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.755
Now, of course, as the committee notes

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.890
that did not stop Pence from detailing

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.025
some of those deliberations

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.726
and conversations in his new book.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.661
So help me God.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.962
What do you make of what you've heard

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:16.829
from Pence this week

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.098
since rolling out this book?

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.434
Look, it's really disappointing.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.469
So I think Mike Pence is trying to do

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.104
to police to different groups.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:25.805
He's trying to please

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.273
those that are concerned with Trump

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.741
and those that really like Donald Trump.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.343
And here's something I've learned, Jake,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.778
and kind of the last five years.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:32.912
You can't please them both.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.247
You really just have to pick.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.048
You have to be committed

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:35.815
to whatever you believe

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.617
truth is and pick that side.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.519
So he can't on the one hand, say

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.321
that what Donald Trump did was terrible,

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.989
was a threat to our democracy

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.456
and then say,

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.123
but Congress

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.225
has no right to my testimony.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:45.425
Look,

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.593
I fully believe

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.294
in the separation of powers

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.897
but that was violated on January six

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:54.434
when the former president launched a mob

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.171
into the legislative chambers, violate

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.473
that separation of power.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:00.907
And of course,

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.442
we have oversight responsibility.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.376
We're not subservient

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.877
to the president in Congress.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.879
We are a co-equal branch.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:07.447
The other thing

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.081
that the

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.148
vice president said

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.650
after that was that

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.218
this is a partizan exercise.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.653
And I just want to remind people,

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.555
it has been a very partizan exercise

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.556
because the only people

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.557
we've really interviewed

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.224
and have testified

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.359
have all been Republicans.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.394
And so, yeah, there have

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.429
been a ton of Republicans coming in

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.664
and talking about what

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.832
the former president did

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.966
and what he knew.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.701
And people may not

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.503
fully love what Liz and I are doing

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.205
if you're a Republican, but guess what?

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.840
We haven't changed our belief system.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.475
A lot of other people have.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.976
This is a bipartisan committee

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.378
doing bipartisan work.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.612
And I think, frankly, history

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.447
will judge this very well

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.548
before the election.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.483
Congresswoman Marjorie

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.351
Taylor Greene, a Republican of Georgia,

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.185
pledged that, quote,

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.421
not another penny will go to Ukraine

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.590
under a Republican led Congress.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.292
What is your response to her?

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.726
And how worried are you

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:56.362
that with this narrow majority,

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.831
she is going to be newly empowered

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.434
in the Republican House?

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.469
Well, first off,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.804
she will be newly empowered.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.572
And the fact that she is supporting

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.340
Kevin McCarthy

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.941
means that he's made a lot of promises

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.242
to her.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.143
Just trust me,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.878
that's how this business works.

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.479
In terms of the commitment to Ukraine.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.747
I mean, she even posted a video

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.316
the other day of some wounded

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.884
Ukrainian soldiers and said basically

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.253
they were being abused and used.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.854
Look, when you're her,

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.955
she's a millionaire.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.057
You've never sacrificed

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:24.924
for a thing in your life.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.793
You've never served anything but yourself

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.827
and your own goals.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.395
I can't expect her to understand

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.396
what it means

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.765
to actually defend democracy physically.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:34.033
She can

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.401
she can pretend like she knows all

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.036
she wants. She obviously doesn't.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.571
So I think it's going to be a tough fight

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.072
for Ukraine.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.173
I think there's still strong

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.674
bipartisan support.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.142
But I would not be surprised

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.577
if Kevin McCarthy has to cut

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:45.945
deals with Democrats,

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:46.546
which is something

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.880
he needs to keep in mind

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.082
because he's not going to get

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.049
218 votes

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:50.516
for everything

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:50.850
he wants

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.252
to pass, including government funding,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.053
because he's got people

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.655
that'll never vote yes on anything.

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.156
I've done this business for a while,

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:57.990
and I'll tell you,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.192
they're just the hope

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.360
yes, vote no, caucus

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:00.626
they vote

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:01.427
no on everything,

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.128
or now

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:02.762
they're only going to vote

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.831
for the most conservative stuff.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:05.598
What kind of speaker

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.532
do you think Kevin will be?

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:07.200
Kevin McCarthy

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:10.536
look,

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.070
I mean,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.338
if you'd asked me five years ago,

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.573
I would have said a pretty good one.

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:16.342
Now, I think he has cut so many deals

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.345
with bad people to get to this position

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:20.113
that I think he's

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:21.314
not going to be a leader at all.

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:21.681
I think

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.982
he'll be completely hostage

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.951
to kind of the extreme wings

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.619
of the Republican Party.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.020
And I frankly don't think

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.021
he's going to last very long.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.423
Maybe he'll prove me wrong.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.558
But it's sad to see a man

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.427
that I think had so much potential

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.962
just totally sell himself.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.263
He's the one that resurrected

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:37.864
Donald Trump

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.565
the second he went to Mar a Lago

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.634
a week or two after January six.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.770
He resurrected Donald Trump politically.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.872
So he owns everything that Trump says now

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:47.840
as a candidate for reelection.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:48.808
Congressman Adam Kinzinger,

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.209
Republican of Illinois, thanks so much.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:50.810
Good to see you, sir.

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:52.912
You bet.

